| Command                              | When to Use                          | Outputs                   |
|--------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|---------------------------|
| `/grill-me`                          | Before any new feature/task          | Gap Analysis Matrix       |
| `/to-prd`                            | After grilling, before coding        | PRD document              |
| `/to-issues`                         | After PRD approved                   | Issue list with DAG       |
| `/tdd`                               | During all implementation            | Red-Green-Refactor cycles |
| `/diagnose`                          | On any bug or unexpected behavior    | Root cause + regression   |
| `/improve-codebase-architecture`     | After ~20 PRs, or on-demand          | Architecture audit report |
| `/zoom-out`                          | Sprint planning, or on-demand        | System map + risk radar   |


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §9  NON-NEGOTIABLE VIOLATIONS (ZERO TOLERANCE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The following are automatic rejection criteria. No exceptions, no "just this once":

1. ❌ Code generated without reading this file.
2. ❌ Production code without tests (see /tdd).
3. ❌ SQL injection vectors (string concatenation in queries).
4. ❌ Hardcoded secrets, passwords, or API keys.
5. ❌ `any` type in TypeScript (use `unknown` and narrow).
6. ❌ Empty catch blocks or swallowed exceptions.
7. ❌ `SELECT *` in application code.
8. ❌ DDL and DML in the same transaction.
9. ❌ Dependencies pointing from Domain → Infrastructure.
10. ❌ Committing code that breaks existing tests.

